            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0318" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-09T17:00:00+08:00">December 9, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 9—1:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>132. My 130, December 8, 2 p.m. The following telegram has been sent to the
                    Legation: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 9, 4 p.m. My December 8, 2 p.m. I sent Consul Lewis Clark to
                            Sinyangchow this morning to cooperate with and advise Dr. Skinsnes in
                            connection with efforts to release Reverend Nelson and his co-worker
                            Tvedt.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
